# Laprdus: Slovenian speech symbols that correct NVDA's own table.
# NVDA's locale/sl/symbols.dic gives the Slovenian quotation marks » and «
# the level "none", so they are spoken at every punctuation level, even
# with punctuation off; every other quotation mark, and these two in the
# English table, have the level "most". A listener reported them spoken
# with the punctuation off (2026-11-03). The names are NVDA's own without
# the stray English word "double".
#
# The hyphen and the em dash are not preserved in NVDA's Slovenian table,
# while the Croatian, Serbian, Bosnian and English tables preserve them
# ("most always"): below the level "most" NVDA turned them into spaces in
# Slovenian alone, so a synthesizer got "2 krat", "10 letnica", "2 3 dni"
# and "1991 2000" for 2-krat, 10-letnica, 2-3 dni and 1991-2000 (found
# 2026-11-23). They keep NVDA's Slovenian names and level and are preserved
# as in the other tables. NVDA applies this dictionary to every synthesizer
# that speaks Slovenian, as it applies its own table.
symbols:
«	dvojni začetni narekovaj	most	always
»	dvojni zaključni narekovaj	most	always
-	kratka črtica	most	always
—	črtica	most	always
